<score-partwise version="4.0">
  <work><work-title>Engraving fixture: content between the staves of a grand staff (015 R-4)</work-title></work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="arranger">Musicanyya test fixture</creator>
    <rights>CC0-1.0 (test fixture, original work)</rights>
    <encoding><software>Musicanyya</software><encoding-date>2026-09-29</encoding-date></encoding>
  </identification>
  <part-list>
    <score-part id="P1"><part-name>Piano</part-name></score-part>
  </part-list>
  <part id="P1">
  <!--
  Feature 015 fixture (tasks.md T025, requested by the notation review in research.md R-4): an eight-bar
  piano piece in C major, 4/4, divisions=4 (eighth=2, quarter=4), whose purpose is to crowd the space
  BETWEEN the two staves of a grand staff, so that the compact vertical spacing (ENGRAVING_SPACING_BRACE_GROUP)
  can be checked for collisions: Verovio must push the staves apart wherever this content needs more room
  than the minimum gap. At the default spacing it engraves without a collision (Verovio 6.3.0, checked by
  the notation review), so a collision seen with the compact spacing is caused by it. Right hand = voice 1
  on staff 1; left hand = voice 5 on staff 2 (and on staff 1 where it crosses), plus voice 6 in M5. Every
  dynamic and hairpin is a direction on staff 1 with placement="below", which is where piano dynamics are
  printed: between the staves. Pedal marks are on staff 2, placement="below", line="yes" (bracket style,
  no "Ped." sign); a pedal change is written as a stop followed by a start at the same moment, because
  Verovio 6.3.0 drops a pedal line that contains type="change", so it is drawn as two brackets with a small
  gap, not as a notch. Every eighth group carries explicit beam elements.
  At 1920 px wide Verovio puts M1-M4 in system 1 and M5-M8 in system 2. In system 1 the staves move closer
  with the compact spacing, down to what the cross-staff beams of M3 need; in system 2 the up-stemmed LH
  beam of M5 with the crescendo over it sets the gap, wider than the default minimum, so it is the same at both spacings.

  M1  p. RH E5 quarter (slur start), D5 C5 eighths, D5 half (slur stop). LH broken chords C3 G3 C4 G3
      (C major) then B2 G3 D4 G3 (G major); C4 and D4 sit on and above the first ledger line above the
      bass staff. Pedal line: pressed on beat 1, changed on beat 3.
  M2  crescendo hairpin from beat 1 to the barline. RH falling scale G4 F4 E4 D4, C4 quarter,
      B3 A3 eighths: ledger-line notes below the treble staff (A3 on the second ledger line). LH F2 half,
      G2 half. Pedal released on beat 1.
  M3  no dynamic or hairpin in this bar (a hairpin here crosses the
      cross-staff beams, and an mf on beat 1 touches the first beam, both already at the default spacing:
      Verovio 6.3.0 does not avoid cross-staff beams). RH half rest, E5 half. LH one voice,
      eighths with a CROSS-STAFF beam in each half: A2 E3 on staff 2, then C4 E4 on staff 1 (beam begins on
      staff 2, ends on staff 1); A4 E4 on staff 1, then C4 A3 on staff 2 (beam begins on staff 1, ends on
      staff 2). Pedal pressed on beat 1.
  M4  mf. RH F5 E5 D5 B4 quarters. LH D3 A3 D4 F4, G2 D3 B3 F4: ledger-line notes above the bass staff (F4
      above the second ledger line). Pedal changed on beats 1 and 3.
  M5  p on beat 1, crescendo hairpin from beat 3 into M6. RH A3 C4 E4 half-note chord (two ledger lines
      below the treble staff), C5 E5 quarters. LH in two voices: voice 6 holds A2 for the whole bar; voice 5
      rests for two beats (a forward) and then plays G3 C4 E4 C4 eighths with stems up, so their stems and
      beam reach into the space between the staves right under the crescendo, and C4 and E4 add ledger
      lines above the bass staff. Pedal changed on beat 1.
  M6  f (the crescendo ends here). Clef change in the bass: staff 2 switches to a G clef on beat 1. RH G5
      E5 quarters, C6 half. LH E4 G4 C5 G4 twice, in the treble clef. Pedal released on beat 1.
  M7  diminuendo hairpin from beat 1 to the last eighth. RH A5 F5 D5 B4 quarters. LH F4 A4 C5 A4 in the
      G clef, then the clef changes back to F on beat 3 and the LH continues G3 D3 B2 G2; one slur runs from
      F4 over the clef change to G2. Pedal line: pressed on beat 1, changed on beat 3.
  M8  p. RH C5 E5 G5 dotted-half chord, quarter rest. LH C2 C3 dotted-half octave, quarter rest. Pedal
      changed on beat 1, released on beat 4 with the rests. Final light-heavy barline.
  -->
